{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d078ef6781167ad064cf6da48c6ae0fd56b267b5736efac0fe48bbacc8a874ab","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconcile Bridge observability and alerting","key_entities":[".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","infra/terraform/iam_bridge_metrics.tf","infra/terraform/monitoring_bridge.tf","rebar/host namespace","bridge_run_failures metric","rebar-bridge-metrics role","rebar-bridge-run-failures alarm","aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github","cloudwatch:PutMetricData","AWS_BRIDGE_METRICS_ROLE_ARN","AWS_BRIDGE_METRICS_REGION"],"problem_keywords":["github actions","cloudwatch","observability","bridge failure","monitoring","alarm","oidc","iam","metric publishing"],"propositions":["Reconcile Bridge run failures on GitHub Actions produce no CloudWatch signal because the bridge runs outside the monitored host infrastructure.","GitHub Actions workflow must publish bridge_run_failures metric to CloudWatch namespace rebar/host, with value 1 on failure and 0 on success, authenticated via OIDC using a narrowly-scoped IAM role.","A new CloudWatch alarm on bridge_run_failures must trigger on the second failure within one hour (period 3600s, threshold 1) to distinguish transient blips from sustained outages like expired tokens.","IAM role rebar-bridge-metrics must grant only cloudwatch:PutMetricData action constrained by cloudwatch:namespace = rebar/host condition, federating the existing GitHub OIDC provider."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787879188387745001,"uuid":"1be5501f-00a9-421b-8b02-a6a492079b84"}